  "direction": "Low-N regression on the GB1 four-site landscape. Download the GB1 four-site data (about 150k variants, one CSV from the FLIP repository). Compare one-hot ridge, one-hot with pairwise epistasis features, a Gaussian process and a small CNN trained on N = 48, 96, 384, 2000 random or single / double-mutant-only variants. Measure Spearman and top-100 recall on the remaining variants over 5 draws. Keep it a small CPU study with reimplemented baselines, at least 5 seeds where cheap, and report negative or mixed results plainly.",
